  "scope": {
    "components": "Two actual pure-signature one-world Henkin component models with opposite quoted structural-CH witnesses are explicit hypotheses. Their existence is not established by this target. Component relational domains are preserved rather than replaced by external powersets.",
    "countermodel": "Conditional on those components, their coalesced model fails the specified CH noncontingency sentence. The boxed-Barcan variant additionally assumes inhabited component domains at every type.",
    "maximalism": "For a closed indicated type, the component hypotheses yield inconsistency of pure Maximalism together with that CH-noncontingency sentence, and likewise with its schema. This does not establish inconsistency of Maximalism alone.",
    "atomicity": "The audit includes admitted singleton intensions in each one-world component and their coalescence, plus Atomicity and boxed Atomicity at every relational type under the stated model hypotheses. No external full-domain premise is substituted.",
    "projection": "Projection/image characterizations and cylinder lifts are certified set-level lemmas. Their full object-language rigidity bridge is a separate obligation."
  },
